SUMMARY:90 Minutes of Innovation: Networks\, Intelligence & the Future of D
 ecision-Making 
LOCATION:The Pub
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 11 spots lef
 t\nStatus: You are Confirmed\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/
 events/180910\n\n1:00PM Program\, 2:30PM Networking\nWhat can we learn fro
 m the individuals shaping AI\, enterprise transformation\, and modern engi
 neering at the highest levels?\n\nIn the latest edition of 90 Minutes of I
 nnovation\, John Werner - venture capitalist\, MIT lecturer\, and Forbes A
 I columnist - will lead a series of one-on-one conversations with three re
 markable leaders\, each offering a distinct perspective on innovation\, le
 adership\, and the moment we’re in.\n\nJon Hirschtick\, founder of Solid
 Works and Onshape\, is a pioneering force in computer-aided design who has
  transformed how engineers and designers build the world. An MIT alumnus\,
  he used winnings from the Institute’s legendary blackjack team to launc
 h his first company - an experience that later inspired the film 21.\n\nSa
 ndy Pentland\, MIT professor with appointments at MIT and Stanford\, and o
 ne of the most cited data scientists globally\, whose work on human behavi
 or\, social networks\, and “reality mining” has fundamentally reshaped
  how we understand trust\, cities\, and collective intelligence. He will s
 peak on his recent book\, Shared Wisdom: Cultural Evolution in the Age of
  AI.\n\nDavid Kenny\, Executive Chairman of Nielsen and former CEO of IBM 
 Watson\, with prior leadership roles at Akamai and The Weather Channel\, h
 as operated at the forefront of AI\, data\, and global enterprise transfor
 mation.\n\nThrough individual interviews\, the afternoon will explore thei
 r personal journeys\, the ideas that have defined their work\, and how eac
 h sees the rapidly evolving landscape of AI\, technology\, and innovation 
 today. Expect an engaging\, insight-rich experience that connects lived ex
 perience with forward-looking perspective - offering a rare window into ho
 w these leaders think\, build\, and lead.\n\n*This event is complimentary 
 and reserved for members only. Light bites and refreshments will be served
 .
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/180910
